;; The net/http corpus's non-passes before net/http is listed (doc/go/NET-HTTP-SURVEY.md, "As built: NH1"):
;; the classes every program of bin/goi check --corpus nethttp that does not pass falls into, in
;; test/goi/divergences.edn's format (a program's class is the first whose :match finds "RESULT REASON";
;; bin/goi divergences --nethttp checks the reference test/nethttp/check-linux-amd64.edn against them,
;; test/goi/divergences.ae). This is the baseline of NH1: net/http interpreted from its embedded forms,
;; as GR8a made it importable. All four classes are :deferred: NH2 (a) lists net/http, its sub-packages and
;; their dependencies compiled, and NH3 runs the corpus on the listed package; the classes then go,
;; or the ones that remain are by design. Read with the Clojure reader.
[
 {:id :interpreted-methods
  :title "an interpreted net/http type has no methods when its value is called through an interface"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "with net/http unlisted its unexported types (*http.response, *http.body, *http.connReader) are goi's interpreted types; the first call of Header, Write, Read, Flush ... on one of them from a handler, from compiled std (fmt, io) or from an interface assertion finds an empty method set (reflect's NumMethod of *http.response is 0), the server's recover logs it, the connection is reset"
  :decided "NH0, NH2 (a): net/http listed compiled"
  :match [#"has no method" #"is not http\.\w+: missing method"]}
 {:id :stub-slots
  :title "a compiled caller of an interpreted net/http method with no stub left"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the families Read, SetDeadline and Addr have 16 stub slots (go/arbace/gotable.edn :stubs) and net/http's interpreted types alone use them up; the call panics (NH7 is about the compiled case)"
  :decided "NH0, NH2 (a), NH7 (a)"
  :match [#"no stub left"]}
 {:id :connection-reset
  :title "the client sees the connection reset by a server whose handler panicked"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "the same cause as :interpreted-methods, seen from the client: the program's own output ends with the transport's error (a reset, an EOF) where gc's has the response, and the panic is in the log the program discards"
  :decided "NH0, NH2 (a)"
  :match [#"^fail status 0 \(gc 0\), stdout differs$"]}
 {:id :hang
  :title "a program that waits for a request that never arrived"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "a handler panic leaves a channel the program waits on unsent; the check's wall cap (90 s) ends it"
  :decided "NH0, NH2 (a)"
  :match [#"^error timeout"]}
]
